WEBVTT

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.150
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:08.770
The Light Ignis thought 
the Ignis were imperfect.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.290
So he created a new vessel known as Bohman.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:16.140
That data was in the simulation.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:26.440
Your future with humans affects all simulations, 
leading to the annihilation of both humans and Ignis.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:34.750
As you said, I started thinking that Ignis were 
immature programs due to the simulation's results.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:40.820
I don't accept that I'm 
inferior to the other Ignis!

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.340
That’s why I created Bohman.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.530
To make up for our flaws.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.000
You must be joking!

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.230
That’s why you got us 
involved in this fight?

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:55.050
It’s your fault that everyone is gone!

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:58.940
Earth!  Windy!  Aqua!  Flame!

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.100
No problem with that.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.910
In the end, we'll all be reborn as one.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:12.480
Light Ignis, free will is something 
that's too much for you to handle.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:22.170
I’ll show you that if evil walks the path 
of selfishness, it'll lead to a foolish future!

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:45.300
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:52.090
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:59.410
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:05.980
Sharing hope for the future

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:12.730
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:19.960
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:26.670
I want to share your pain

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:02.230
Revolver’s ace monster is out!

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:05.660
It's such an exciting monster!

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:09.260
Deal a huge blow to Lightning!

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.130
Should you say that, Boss?

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:13.920
The media must be neutral.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.310
Borreload Dragon’s effect!

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:18.700
Anti Enemy Varrett!

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:24.720
One monster loses 500 ATK and DEF!

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.750
You can’t activate any card 
effects against this effect!

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.860
Here I go!  Battle!

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:38.030
Borreload Dragon attacks Plumbum Trident!

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.440
Thunder Varrel Cannon!

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.880
Yeah!  He destroyed it!

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:55.140
But couldn't he have used Borreload's 
effect to steal a monster?

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:59.150
If he stole Plumbum Trident, 
its ATK would be halved.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.700
And he'd deal 1100 damage.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:07.190
I see!  His attack dealt more 
damage by not using the effect.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:12.570
How logical.  That attack made sense.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:16.940
But since you’re logical, it's 
easy to figure out your plans.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.620
What?

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:23.170
You’re helping my strategy.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:27.650
Plumbum Trident’s effect 
activates from the graveyard!

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:35.000
When it's destroyed in battle, I can add 
Judgment Arrows from my deck to my hand.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:42.290
Now I have the card I want in my hand.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.740
So this battle was a trap.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:49.030
In order for Lightning 
to get Judgment Arrows.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:52.270
That monster had that effect?

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:55.850
Next, Plumbum Trident’s effect.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:05:02.610
When it's destroyed, I can place it in 
the Spell & Trap Zone as a Link Spell.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:07.350
When it leaves the field, it's banished.

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:09.820
A new Link Spell…

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:14.060
That's why its markers face that way.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:18.100
A Link Spell other than Judgment Arrows!

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:22.180
This is bad.  Lightning 
doesn’t make mistakes.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:30.280
I'm the one who'll show which of 
us walks the path of foolishness.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:35.280
I set one card and end my turn.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:39.780
Lightning already has 
Judgment Arrows in his hand.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:43.960
How he deals with it will 
determine who wins this duel.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:47.690
Revolver needs to hang tough for now.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:50.660
My turn!  I draw!

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:55.670
I activate the Link Spell, 
Plumbum Trident’s effect!

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:00.050
It has another effect?

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:01.870
What kind of effect?

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:06.020
I return one Link Monster in the 
graveyard to the Extra Deck...

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:12.240
...to Special Summon an Armatos Legio Link 
Monster from the graveyard next to its link.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:18.040
I return Decurion to my deck 
and Special Summon Centurion.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:25.160
The Field Spell, Armatos 
Colosseum’s effect!

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:27.900
I send Sica from my hand to the graveyard...

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:34.400
...to Special Summon Armatos Legio 
Segmentata and Gladius next to Centurion’s link!

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:38.610
Appear!  The circuit that guides the light!

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:43.550
The summoning condition is one 
Level 4 or lower Armatos Legio!

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.280
Link Summon!

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:50.390
Appear!  Link 1 Armatos Legio Centurion!

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:55.640
Now Lightning has a Link Marker that 
points to the Spell & Trap Zone.

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:59.860
He can activate Judgment Arrows!

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:03.100
You’re about to see hell, Revolver.

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.640
An AI is talking about hell?

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.330
What’s so funny?

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:11.800
You’re the one who’ll 
see hell, Light Ignis!

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:17.420
Judgment Arrows is a terrifying card 
that changes the course of battle.

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:22.290
Do you think I'd only have 
one way to deal with it?

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:27.060
I activate the trap, Mind Crush!

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.650
I declare a card name.

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:35.620
If that card is in your hand, you 
must discard all copies of that card!

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:40.240
I declare Judgment Arrows!

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:52.620
How dare you get rid of my Judgment Arrows!

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.970
Well done, Revolver!

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:57.840
Impressive.  He thought this far ahead.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:03.560
Lightning didn’t think Revolver 
was thinking two steps ahead.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:05.360
Serves him right.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.440
Then I’ll just make you succumb with power!

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:12.840
Appear!  The circuit that guides the light!

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:17.310
The summoning conditions are 
at least three Armatos Legio!

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.680
Link Summon!

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:24.380
Link 4 Armatos Legio Magnus Dux!

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:31.010
I activate Segmentata’s 
effect from my graveyard!

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:35.910
When it's linked and sent to the 
graveyard for a Link Summon,

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:38.800
I can pay 1000 LP to activate it!

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:43.520
All monsters used to Link 
Summon return to my deck!

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:53.480
And for each of Magnus Dux's Link Markers, 
I return a card in my graveyard to my deck.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.960
Magnus Dux has four Link Markers.

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.950
He has five cards in his graveyard.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:06.460
I return Speculata, Gladius and two 
Sicas from my graveyard to my deck.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:13.200
Then you select a card in my 
graveyard and add it to my hand.

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:17.900
There's only one card in my graveyard.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.740
Judgment Arrows.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.470
That’s right.

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:28.950
As you said, Judgment Arrows is a terrifying 
card that changes the course of battle.

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:34.190
Did you think I'd only have 
one way to deal with it?

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:37.980
Now choose your destiny.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.900
So you can’t choose your own destruction.

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:46.220
You're wasting time.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:51.040
I'll add the remaining card to my hand.

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:56.470
Judgment Arrows has 
returned to my hand again.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:59.710
He’s in a huge pinch again!

00:09:59.710 --> 00:10:03.850
But Lightning paid a lot for it.

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:06.340
We still don’t know the outcome.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:12.690
True, it’s hard to believe 
that Revolver will lose easily.

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:16.430
I activate the Link Spell, Judgment Arrows!

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:20.930
Appear!  The three arrows 
that judge the world!

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:24.470
Battle!

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:28.840
Magnus Dux attacks Borreload Dragon!

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:31.960
At this moment, Borreload’s effect!

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:34.100
Anti Enemy Varrett!

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:41.070
Magnus Dux's effect negates the activation 
and destroys a Link Monster’s effect.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:44.730
But it can’t activate 
against Borreload’s effect!

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:53.360
But against Magnus Dux’s overwhelming 
power, all monsters are nothing more than weaklings!

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:55.420
Judgment Arrows’s effect!

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:59.640
Since Magnus Dux is linked 
to it, its ATK are doubled!

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:11.420
The battle is over.  Magnus 
Dux’s ATK return to normal.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.420
Lightning has 1700 LP.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:16.440
Revolver has 2000 LP.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:21.890
Revolver has more LP, but 
he’s at a huge disadvantage.

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:28.630
I created Judgment Arrows to 
open the door to a new world.

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:32.600
A monkey like you can’t destroy it.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:34.120
Monkey?

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:37.640
Lightning, is that how you view humans?

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:39.940
You have a problem with that?

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:44.620
We don’t need humans.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:46.290
Don’t need them?

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:50.590
You’re talking just like Windy!

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:52.220
Exactly.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:56.190
Of course it has the same 
personality as the Wind Ignis.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.160
What do you mean?

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.160
Just as I said.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:04.640
The Wind Ignis and it are the same.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:08.200
Remember what the Fire Ignis said?

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:13.640
How it's strange that the Wind Ignis’s 
personality had become extreme?

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:14.380
What?

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:19.290
You didn't used to be this twisted.

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:21.520
What happened?

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:24.490
Nothing happened.  This is me.

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:31.570
As Flame said, Windy used 
to be easy to talk to.

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:35.470
But it’s like something inside him changed.

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:41.440
Exactly.  Because his true 
personality was altered.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:49.120
His personality was altered?

00:12:52.540 --> 00:13:00.760
Does that mean Windy’s 
program was rewritten?

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.390
Exactly.

00:13:02.390 --> 00:13:04.610
Who would do that?

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:05.500
You can’t mean-

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.470
I do.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:15.240
Light Ignis, in order to advance 
your Ignis unification plan...

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:20.980
...you rewrote the Wind Ignis’s 
program to force it to be your ally.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:23.720
I already checked the records.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:29.450
In the Wind Ignis’s simulations, there 
were no models of an evil personality.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:34.160
In other words, an outsider changed it.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:39.030
Lightning is the source of Windy’s evil.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:47.170
So that curse was also…

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:50.840
Yes.  I set it.

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:53.920
I expected Windy to lose.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:57.380
That’s the only way he was useful.

00:13:57.380 --> 00:13:59.540
You must be joking, Lightning!

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:01.620
You’ll go that far?

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:04.090
Everything is for you all!

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:07.090
For the future of the Ignis!

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:09.960
For the future?  Stop joking!

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:14.430
Everything you do is full of lies!

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:19.570
And we trusted you to be our leader?

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:21.520
You shouldn't regret it.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:26.970
It may have started as a lie, but my ideas 
are heading towards the correct future.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:31.580
Humans will eventually be under 
AI’s control and vanish.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:36.050
It's an unopposable program called destiny!

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:38.850
That’s how you’re justifying it?

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:41.130
Don’t feel so proud, Light Ignis!

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:47.000
If we solely focus on the growth of 
memories, AIs are superior to humans.

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:49.500
But not as a species.

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:53.470
On that point, my father’s 
ideas were wrong.

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:56.920
You are spineless as a species.

00:14:57.970 --> 00:14:59.970
Humans are different.

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:02.950
We evolved as creatures of flesh and blood.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:06.420
Our flesh is full of life!

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:11.390
I always felt that when I was 
taking care of my father.

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:16.290
Humans know and fear death because 
it's engraved in our DNA.

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:20.870
So we celebrate the limited time 
we have and chase our dreams!

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:25.570
Bone, flesh and time limit your species.

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:28.440
But they don't tie me down!

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:33.340
We’re a new species that 
exceed your expectations!

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:39.320
Then I'll mercilessly and 
completely correct you!

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:41.610
Go ahead and try!

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:46.790
Not that you can because I 
have Judgment Arrows's power!

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:52.570
Fine!  Light Ignis, it’s 
time for you to vanish!

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:54.370
My turn!

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:55.830
I draw!

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:59.730
I activate the Field Spell, 
Boot Sector Launch’s effect!

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:07.130
If you have more monsters 
on the field than I do...

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:12.760
...I Special Summon Rokkets from my 
graveyard equal to the difference in defense position.

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:16.090
Resurrect, Magnarokket Dragon!

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:23.500
Then I summon Estrangement 
Dragon from my hand!

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:28.860
That's what you're doing?  
Summoning a weakling?

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:36.140
Since I have Judgment Arrows, you need a 
monster with at least 5000 ATK to defeat me.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.140
Then I’ll show you!

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:41.880
The moment where humanity's dueling 
surpasses your expectations!

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:45.350
Estrangement Dragon’s effect activates!

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:51.750
When it's summoned, I Special Summon 
a new Estrangement Dragon from

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:55.140
my deck on your field in attack position!

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:57.800
My field?

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:03.020
If there’s another monster 
other than itself in play,

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:05.040
Estrangement Dragon can’t be attacked.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:10.780
And when an effect Special Summons it, 
it’s sent to the graveyard at the end of the turn.

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:13.780
What's Revolver planning to do?

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:17.010
Two Level 4 monsters…  Can it be?

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:25.820
I use Level 4 Estrangement Dragon and 
Magnarokket Dragon to build the Overlay Network!

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:35.810
When two soaring, heroic 
roars merge into thunder,

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:39.760
it opens the eternal door 
and shows its power!

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:42.810
Xyz Summon!

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:52.120
Appear, Rank 4 Borreload eXcharge Dragon!

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:58.640
Revolver had a new secret weapon ready.

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:01.930
He does the unexpected as usual.

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:07.160
A Rank 4 with 3000 ATK?  That’s crazy!

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:10.480
An Xyz Monster.

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:14.140
But that’s not enough to defeat me!

00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:20.140
The fact that you think so highly of 
yourself proves you’re shallow, Light Ignis.

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:24.380
Borreload eXcharge Dragon’s 
effect activates!

00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:27.120
Anti Enemy eXcharge!

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:31.360
I use one Overlay Unit.

00:18:32.660 --> 00:18:36.810
One monster loses 600 ATK.

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:40.300
I select Magnus Dux!

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:46.040
Additionally, I can Special Summon 
a Borrel monster from my graveyard!

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:49.040
Resurrect, Borreload Dragon!

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:53.110
Here I go, Light Ignis!

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:58.380
Borreload eXcharge Dragon attacks Magnus Dux!

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:02.120
Borreload Dragon’s effect activates!

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:05.090
Anti Enemy Varrett!

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:09.330
Magnus Dux’s ATK decreased!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:12.280
Judgment Arrows’s effect!

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:18.000
But it’s less than 
Borreload eXcharge’s ATK!

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:22.850
Take this!  Thunder Varrel Cannon!

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:41.560
All right!  He destroyed Magnus Dux!

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:49.470
Due to eXcharge's effect, I can’t 
attack you directly this turn.

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:55.470
I see.  That’s why you summoned 
Estrangement on my field!

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:57.350
Exactly!

00:19:57.350 --> 00:20:01.010
Borreload Dragon has 3000 ATK.

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:05.090
Estrangement Dragon has 1500 ATK.

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:08.090
And you have 1500 LP!

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:10.730
Revolver is on point!

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:14.560
All right!  If this attack 
succeeds, Revolver wins!

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:18.800
Lightning can't stop this attack.

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:22.850
Boss!  The duel is finally going to end!

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:24.800
Well done, Revolver!

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:27.040
He’s a bad guy, but he does justice.

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:30.010
He's a dark hero!

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:37.610
This is the end, Light Ignis!

00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:40.180
Return to nothing!

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:45.720
Borreload Dragon attacks Estrangement Dragon-

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:48.800
What?

00:21:09.980 --> 00:21:12.220
What did you do, Lightning?

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:37.540
